    "snippet": "---\ntitle: The Top 100 Marketing Executives of 2022\nauthor: Jcarlos\ndate: 2022-02-14\n---\nAlumni Spotlight is pleased to announce the Top 100 Marketing Executives of 2022. These individuals are the driving force behind much of their company's brand and market positioning success. As a result of the pandemic, marketing executives across all industries have had to adjust their strategies and employ tactics to maintain brand awareness in today's ever-changing environment. These awardees employ years of experience and creativity to ensure their companies remain at the forefront of their respective markets.\n\nAwardee Lisa Gevelber, the Chief Marketing Officer for Google, has been a part of the company for nearly 12 years and founded Grow with Google where she has helped more than 6 million Americans develop their businesses, careers and skills all online. Microsoft's Chief Marketing Officer and Executive Vice President, Chris Capossela, plays a big impact on driving revenue, growth and share across the company's consumer business by leading with his decades of experience. Meanwhile, awardee Suzy DePrizio, the Chief Marketing Officer of Centene, plays a crucial role in the company's market strategy, advertising and brand position so the company can continue to reach individuals across the nation and provide high quality and cost effective healthcare to them.\n\nThere is no indication of a decline for a growing need for talented marketing executives. In fact, research indicates that marketing challenges will continue as audience attention becomes more fragmented across all types of media channels. This year's awardees are best positioned to lead their companies towards sustainable growth and marketing innovation. Please join us in celebrating the achievements of the Top 100 Marketing Executive of 2022.\n\n2. Dustin Sedgwick\n\nChief Marketing Officer - Payments, J.P. Morgan\n\nPrinceton University\n\nDustin Sedgwick is the Chief Marketing Officer of J.