eans we've excluded, for example, hugely influential foreign action films like The Way of the Dragon and the original Mad Max.\n\nWe've had to neglect extraordinary foreign classics like Pather Panchali and The Lives of Others \u2013 which are not only some of the best low budget films of all time, but the best films of all time period.\n\nEven relatively recent movies made for less than $5 million are edged out if inflation has already pushed their present-day cost past our mark. Such films include Donnie Darko,"
