    "snippet": "---\ntitle: Here's what 60 celebrities looked like in high school\nauthor: Kirsten Acuna\ndate: 2022-10-25\n---\n- If you think the biggest actors were only in drama club and musicals growing up, think again.\n\n- They were cheerleaders, prom kings, and homecoming queens, and even governed their student bodies.\n\n- Insider rounded up what some of the biggest names in Hollywood were up to during their formative years.\n\nHigh school is a wild time in everyone's lives, but have you ever wondered what your favorite celebrities were like during their school years?\n\nClassmates.com and Ancestry.com provided Insider with many high school yearbook photos featuring celebrities, from Ted Danson to Jennifer Lopez, and some of their superlatives.\n\nSome of what we learned about these A-listers was unexpected: \"The Martian\" star Jessica Chastain dropped out of high school, and Bill Murray paid his way through Catholic school.\n\nKeep reading to see what your favorite celebrities were like and what they were doing in high school.\n\nPatricia Arquette rocked a dramatic haircut in high school.\n\nArquette went to Catholic school, and even wanted to become a nun when she grew up, she told NPR.\n\nTed Danson played basketball at his Connecticut boarding school and called himself a \"frustrated athlete.\"\n\nDanson told the Washington Post that he was probably a \"frustrated athlete.\" He continued, \"I mean, I love basketball with a burning passion, it's what got me through high school. I may not be an athlete, but I feel I have the soul of an athlete.\"\n\nJerry Seinfeld graduated from Massapequa High School in Long Island, New York, in the '70s, while rocking a very '70s hairdo.\n\nSeinfeld graduated from high school in 1972. He and fellow Massapequa native Alec Baldwin did an episode of \"Comedians in Cars Getting Coffee\" in their shared hometown, and even paid a visit to their favorite diner.\n\nGwen Stefani has always been interested in music.\n\n\"I was the opposite of rebellious when I was a teen,\" Stefani told Sweety High in 2017. \"I was very peaceful and easy and passive. I always had that one friend and I discovered music. Kind of like everybody, when you find that music that defines who you are, you kind of relate to it.\"\n\nJulia Louis-Dreyfus did theater in high school.\n\nWhile the \"Veep\" star was in"
