 over time;\n\n2. Four readings on the Iolani Palace site, the history of the Hawaiian Islands, and the views of Hawaiian monarchs;\n\n3. Four historic photographs showing the first Iolani Palace, the exterior and interior of the second Iolani Palace, and the landing of U.S. Marines in Honolulu in 1893;\n\n4. One historic political cartoon illustration about American expansionism.\n\nWhere it fits into the curriculum\n\nThe lesson could be used in middle and high school units relating to Hawaiian history, 19th Century American Expansionism, Globalization, Cultural Ex"
